[sliver] The linter's strip metric is the specified 1.5 mm depth of the seam channel and its matching inward fold. These four faces turn a constant 2.38 mm casing section through the channel; the 1.5 mm face dimension is the recess depth, rather than a 1.5 mm material ligament. Both channel inside corners are the selected seams' placement surfaces.
alternatives: A 1.6 mm channel leaves this face-width ranking but changes Derek's selected 1.5 mm channel. Sloping the sides removes the axis-aligned face while replacing the inside corners used by the seam placement.
